From: Rafael J. Wysocki (Intel) <rafael@kernel.org>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 21:05:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] PM: sleep: Include runtime callbacks in smart-suspend eligibility

Import the maintainer-proposed attachment from the hibernation PM review.
A device with runtime callbacks is not callback-free just because it lacks
system-wide PM callbacks. Its runtime resources must not be reported active
without the corresponding resume path.

This is the review attachment, not the initially proposed no_pm_callbacks
exception in device_resume_noirq(), which the maintainer identified as
unsafe for runtime-suspended parents of active children. No unrelated wake
IRQ policy changes are included. Native hibernation is not accepted yet.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/CAJZ5v0g3zU51Q4sQvmTNH-Jtycu1D5Qm9c6r2t_DCp03ePzV-g@mail.gmail.com/
---
 drivers/base/power/main.c    |    5 +++--
 drivers/base/power/power.h   |    4 ++++
 drivers/base/power/runtime.c |    6 ++++++
 3 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/base/power/main.c
+++ b/drivers/base/power/main.c
@@ -2179,13 +2179,14 @@ static bool device_prepare_smart_suspend
 
 	/*
 	 * The "smart suspend" feature is enabled for devices whose drivers ask
-	 * for it and for devices without PM callbacks.
+	 * for it and for devices without any PM callbacks (including runtime PM
+	 * callbacks).
 	 *
 	 * However, if "smart suspend" is not enabled for the device's parent
 	 * or any of its suppliers that take runtime PM into account, it cannot
 	 * be enabled for the device either.
 	 */
-	if (!dev->power.no_pm_callbacks &&
+	if ((!dev->power.no_pm_callbacks || pm_runtime_callbacks_exist(dev)) &&
 	    !dev_pm_test_driver_flags(dev, DPM_FLAG_SMART_SUSPEND))
 		return false;
 
--- a/drivers/base/power/power.h
+++ b/drivers/base/power/power.h
@@ -131,6 +131,8 @@ extern void wakeup_source_sysfs_remove(s
 
 extern int pm_wakeup_source_sysfs_add(struct device *parent);
 
+extern bool pm_runtime_callbacks_exist(struct device *dev);
+
 #else /* !CONFIG_PM_SLEEP */
 
 static inline void device_pm_sleep_init(struct device *dev) {}
@@ -160,6 +162,8 @@ static inline int pm_wakeup_source_sysfs
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static inline bool pm_runtime_callbacks_exist(struct device *dev) { return false; }
+
 #endif /* !CONFIG_PM_SLEEP */
 
 static inline void device_pm_init(struct device *dev)
--- a/drivers/base/power/runtime.c
+++ b/drivers/base/power/runtime.c
@@ -2136,4 +2136,10 @@ bool pm_runtime_need_not_resume(struct d
 		 dev->power.ignore_children);
 }
 
+bool pm_runtime_callbacks_exist(struct device *dev)
+{
+	return !dev->power.no_callbacks && (GET_CALLBACK(dev, runtime_resume) ||
+		GET_CALLBACK(dev, runtime_suspend));
+}
+
 #endif /* CONFIG_PM_SLEEP */
